[ ] Route charter markdown writes through EffectBatch delivery $jot, close and update call atomic_write directly and skip the precondition revision check. Confirmed 2026-09-17: this is NOT missing machinery to build from scratch — EffectBatch::preconditions + ResourcePrecondition/ExpectedResource::Revision + validate_preconditions + DeliveryError::Conflict/ResourceConflict already exist and are already enforced for action mutations (clearhead-workspace-fs/src/lib.rs). Charter markdown writes just never route through that seam; bring them onto the same EffectBatch+precondition path actions already use, don't build a second mechanism.$ !3 ^2026-08-31T22:07 #01a05b5d-62be-73c0-8e70-154d78bd57a3
[ ] Let add action create a missing charter actions file $promoting agent-surface failed with has no associated actions file; had to touch next.actions by hand$ ^2026-09-14T17:09 <adopt-unified-root #01a0a266-01cf-73e3-acf2-a669be313387
[ ] Write vdir displayname metadata from charter alias $collection dirs stay stable path keys like plans/next; ClearHead writes the vdir displayname file from the alias and refreshes it on rename, so calendar apps show readable names and vdirsyncer metasync carries them. Cross-workspace uniqueness stays a transport mapping, not a folder name. Decided 2026-09-15$ ^2026-09-15T01:24 #01a0a42b-3bd4-71c1-b922-39b88e9c310b
[ ] Specify or forbid a plan_path shared by several workspaces $each workspace sees the other's collections as unowned-plans-collection, quarantines them, and doctor fix may offer to delete them; every workspace also owns next and inbox collections, so names collide too. Found 2026-09-15$ ^2026-09-15T01:24 #01a0a42b-3be7-7691-bcbf-366e1fd87a77
[ ] Purge journaling text and fix link definitions in workspace spec $workspace.md mutation durability section and archive step still describe the journal and pending recovery that direct-delivery retired; all reference link definitions sit on one line so only the first parses$ ^2026-09-15T01:24 #01a0a42b-3bf3-7423-a374-fc63bfec6d48
[ ] Stop deriving charter ids from titles in parse_charter $a charter md without frontmatter id gets a v5 id recomputed from its title on every load, so a retitle silently changes identity; the concept identity rules forbid live recompute. init sidesteps it via charter_frontmatter_id; loading should report the gap for doctor instead. Found 2026-09-15$ ^2026-09-15T01:55 #01a0a447-8bcd-77b1-bda1-ef3201183590
[x] Drop the retired clearhead-graphd path from config.json's additional_workspaces $graphd was retired; the stale entry made any command scanning all workspace_dirs() without --charter/--file (e.g. delete action) fail with Invalid path instead of just skipping it. Found and fixed while verifying the add/delete VerbOutcome change.$ ^2026-09-17T20:54 #01a0b2a6-b3d3-714d-bb2d-347bd4df4ba5
[ ] Surface DeliveryError\:\:Conflict as a structured VerbError\:\:Conflict $Action mutations already carry a real precondition check (EffectBatch::preconditions, validate_preconditions in clearhead-workspace-fs/src/lib.rs) and already detect a stale-write race as DeliveryError::Conflict{conflict: ResourceConflict{path, expected, actual}}. But lib.rs:492 immediately flattens it via .to_string() into WorkspaceError::Actions(String), so every CLI verb loses the shape and an agent just sees an opaque error, not something it can branch on. Add VerbError::Conflict{path, expected, actual} (or similar) and thread the real ResourceConflict through instead of stringifying it. Found while designing the agent-surface MCP tools: multiple concurrent agents writing through capture/transact is exactly the scenario that turns this from theoretical into routine.$ !3 ^2026-09-17T21:25 #01a0b2c2-f791-733e-b323-6b16f3e7d24a
